\begin{lemma}\label{Lemma0}
Let $\mathcal{G}=\langle G,E\rangle$ be a finite graph,  $L$ be a finite and non-empty set that labels  nodes of $G$ and  $\mathcal{L}:nodes(G)\rightarrow L$ be the labeling function. Assume that $card(L)\leq n^k$ for some $2\leq n$ and $k>1$, $k,n\in \mathbb{N}$, and, suppose that  there is $r\in\mathbb{R}$, $r>1$, such that,
$r^{n^k}<card(\mathcal{G})$. Then , there is at least one $l\in L$, such that, $r^{n^k}<card(\{v/ \mathcal{L}(v)=l\})$.
\end{lemma}
